Check out this flourless high-protein wrap idea 🥰 

Dairy-free and gluten-free, diet-friendly and very nutritious with a spicy kick 😁🌶️ 

This wrap is only 2 WW points! 🥳 

Enjoy it with your favourite fillings! I’ve layered my wrap with harissa paste, spinach, broccoli falafels (recipe in my previous reel), and sriracha sauce. So flavorful! 😋 

Ingredients: 

50gr (1.76 ounces) quinoa 50gr (1.76 ounces) red lentils 125 milliliters (1/2 cup) water 1 chili (optional) Cilantro (optional) 1 garlic clove Salt to taste 

Method: 

Soak both quinoa and red lentils for a couple of hours. By using boiling water, you can accelerate the process if you are short on time. 

When you start with 50 grams (1.75 ounces) each, after soaking, they will both double in weight. 

Rinse and drain both, and add to a food processor with water and the other ingredients. 

Blend at high speed until you get a creamy consistency. 

Let it rest for a few minutes, then transfer to a baking tray lined with parchment paper. 

Bake in a preheated oven at 180°C (350°F) for about 20 minutes and enjoy! 